Subject: [PATCH] mysys: add the WASIX system API implementation

9.x moved the VCPU and cgroup probes into components/library_mysys, with one
implementation per platform selected in CMake. WASIX matches none of them
(UNIX is not set for the WASI system name), so mysqld fails to link with
num_vcpus_using_affinity(), is_running_in_cgroup() and friends undefined.

Add a WASIX implementation: no CPU affinity API, no cgroups, and the VCPU
count from sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN), which is also what the Linux
implementation falls back to.

diff --git a/components/library_mysys/CMakeLists.txt b/components/library_mysys/CMakeLists.txt
index f3b855f0..9667326d 100644
--- a/components/library_mysys/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/components/library_mysys/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -28,12 +28,16 @@ SET(MY_SYSTEM_SOURCES
   my_system_api/my_system_api_common.cc
 )
 
-IF(UNIX)
+# WASIX has neither cgroups nor a CPU affinity API; it gets its own file.
+IF(UNIX AND NOT WASIX)
   LIST(APPEND MY_SYSTEM_SOURCES
     my_system_api/my_system_api_cgroup.cc)
 ENDIF()
 
-IF(LINUX)
+IF(WASIX)
+  LIST(APPEND MY_SYSTEM_SOURCES
+    my_system_api/my_system_api_wasix.cc)
+ELSEIF(LINUX)
   LIST(APPEND MY_SYSTEM_SOURCES
     my_system_api/my_system_api_linux.cc)
 ELSEIF(APPLE)
diff --git a/components/library_mysys/my_system_api/my_system_api_wasix.cc b/components/library_mysys/my_system_api/my_system_api_wasix.cc
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ff542ef4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/components/library_mysys/my_system_api/my_system_api_wasix.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
